              <field>
                <name>SGI_CLEAR_PENDING0</name>
                <description>clear-pending state for SGI [x * 4]
Writing a 1 clears the pending state of the SGI [x * 4] for the corresponding source processor, and no longer targets the processor performing the write.
Writing a 0 has no effect.
Reading a bit identifies whether the SGI [x * 4] is pending, from the corresponding source processor, on the reading processor.</description>
                <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
                <bitWidth>2</bitWidth>
                <access>read-write</access>
              </field>
