                <name>DDRPHYCLPEN</name>
                <description>DDRPHYC peripheral clocks enable during CSleep mode
If DDRPHYC block is configured as secure via the corresponding DECPROT[1] field of the ETZPC register, a write access to this register field must be secure. A read access may be secure or non-secure.
Set and clear by software.
This bit is controlling the gating of dphy_ker_ck and pclk4_dphy in CSleep</description>
                <bitOffset>5</bitOffset>
                <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <enumeratedValues>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>B_0x0</name>
                    <description>means that the peripheral clocks are disabled in CSleep</description>
