            <displayName>RCC_MP_S_AHB4ENSETR</displayName>
            <description>This is a secure register, for enabling the clock of the secure (AHB4) GPIO ports, as defined
by the GPIO register file and more specifically the GPIOxSECCFGR.SECy control bit with
x=A..I, and y = 0..15 (or 2 for x=I). A write access to this register field must be secure. A
read access may be secure or non-secure.
This register is used to set the peripheral clock enable bit of the corresponding peripheral. It
shall be used to allocate a peripheral. Writing '0' has no effect, reading will return the
effective values of the corresponding bits. Writing a '1' sets the corresponding bit to '1'.</description>
